preConditionHook:
// A DIFFICULT TRADING ENVIRONMENT (G07-09): while the market has pressed into
// EITHER Keltner band on at least rideCount of the last rideWindow bars, take
// no new position on either side. Both sides identical -- an OR of the two
// directions, which is what makes this a Switch rather than a mirrored filter:
// ANDed entry panes cannot rebuild an OR.
//
// Kept apart from ClosesOutsideKeltnerBandCount by ROLE, not by formula, on the
// RangeWidthBelowAtrMultiple / TightRangeBlocksEntries precedent. Not
// TightRangeBlocksEntries itself, which blocks in an unusually TIGHT range --
// the opposite condition in the same role. No book numbers: 5 of 8 chosen.
// DIVERGENCE FROM THE BOOK, recorded rather than hidden, exactly as
// TightRangeBlocksEntries records it: the generator's Switch role both blocks
// entries AND forces an exit (strategyWriter.py `_switchLines`). Grimes asks
// only for the block. There is no block-without-flat role; if forcing flat is
// not wanted, place ClosesOutsideKeltnerBandCount NEGATED in each entry pane
// instead, which blocks without forcing flat but only pane by pane.
// While countReady is false the Switch is FALSE: a blocker must not block on a
// warm-up reading.
// THE KELTNER BAND (Grimes merge decision 1, book p68: "2.25 multiples of the
// ATR around a 20-period exponential moving average"). The centre line is
// EXPONENTIAL -- WFSafe_Xaverage, not the simple Average KeltnerChannelCross
// uses. Defaults 20 / 2.25 / 20 are the book's.
//
// MultiWalk's WFSafe_Xaverage, ported from EmaGapBar (the EMA reference, which
// carries the full measurements). EL_XAverage_Probe.txt (@OJ 240min, chart
// starts 2007 and 2010):
//   * BIT-IDENTICAL to the plain XAverage built-in at a fixed length --
//     (wf - xa) * 1e12 printed exactly 0.0000 on all 17,785 bars;
//   * the SEED is the PRICE on the study's first calculated bar
//     (ctx.CurrentBar() == 1), not a length-term simple average;
//   * the recurrence is x + sf*(p - x), ONE statement, never
//     sf*p + (1-sf)*x -- the two separated on 67% of probed bars past 100;
//   * there is NO warm-up hole on the CURRENT value, so no bar-count guard;
//   * an EMA NEVER FORGETS ITS SEED (it decays at (1 - sf)^n, ~330 bars), so
//     Max Bars Back and the chart start are part of this rule's specification.
// LENGTH CHANGE MEASURED 2026-09-17 (EL_XAverage_Lag_Probe.txt): the wrapper
// recomputes sf on the bar the length changes and carries its state, no
// re-seed, so emaLength may be optimized in grids.
// Scratch below is declared in localVariables, not at hook scope: the generator
// only prefixes declared locals, so a hook-scope declaration is a redefinition
// when this rule is placed twice in one strategy.
emaSf = 2.0 / (emaLength + 1.0);
if (ctx.CurrentBar() == 1) {
    emaVal = close[0];
} else {
    emaVal = emaVal + emaSf * (close[0] - emaVal);
}
// WFSafe_AvgTrueRange: MultiWalk's ROLLING accumulator, ported from
// AtrProfitTarget (the reference, with the measurements). Seeded with a full
// sum on the first calculated bar or when the length changes, and updated
// thereafter as TWO statements -- EL evaluates S[1] + in - out left to right,
// and folding it to S += in - out rounds differently (@OJ 2015-02-20).
if (atrSeedLen != (int)atrLength) {
    atrSum = 0.0;
    for (int i = 0; i < (int)atrLength; ++i) {
        double hi = high[i] > close[i + 1] ? high[i] : close[i + 1];
        double lo = low[i] < close[i + 1] ? low[i] : close[i + 1];
        atrSum += hi - lo;
    }
    atrSeedLen = (int)atrLength;
} else {
    const int out = (int)atrLength;
    double hiIn = high[0] > close[1] ? high[0] : close[1];
    double loIn = low[0] < close[1] ? low[0] : close[1];
    double hiOut = high[out] > close[out + 1] ? high[out] : close[out + 1];
    double loOut = low[out] < close[out + 1] ? low[out] : close[out + 1];
    atrSum += hiIn - loIn;
    atrSum -= hiOut - loOut;
}
atr = atrSum / (int)atrLength;
band = bandMult * atr;
upper = emaVal + band;
lower = emaVal - band;
// EL's CountIF counts bars 0..N-1 INCLUDING the current bar and its counted
// condition is a TRUE SERIES (VERIFIED): at position i it tests the band at
// OFFSET i, so every counted bar reads the band as it stood on that bar. The
// zero-initialized ring buffers below supply exactly that. `upper` and `lower`
// are EL VARIABLES, so their [k] history is the value the strategy assigned k
// bars ago and reads 0.0 before that history exists -- MEASURED for the
// function itself (EL_XAverage_Lag_Probe.txt, lag1/lag5 exactly 0 on every bar
// past the lag on both charts) and the same zero-filled pre-history the
// countif row records for variables. The buffers are re-seeded if the depth
// ever changes, the way BarRangeAboveStd's mirrored history is.
// That zero is NEVER compared against: comparing a back-adjusted price with 0
// is a sign test and would fail the shift test, so the rule guards its own
// warm-up on the bar counter instead. Both counts accumulate in ONE pass and
// neither test is short-circuited away, so the loop runs the same number of
// times as EasyLanguage's.
bandDepth = (int)rideWindow;
if (bandDepth < 1) {
    bandDepth = 1;
}
if (upperHistory.size() != (std::size_t)bandDepth) {
    upperHistory.assign((std::size_t)bandDepth, 0.0);
    lowerHistory.assign((std::size_t)bandDepth, 0.0);
    bandCursor = 0;
}
upperHistory[bandCursor] = upper;
lowerHistory[bandCursor] = lower;
rideUpCount = 0;
rideDownCount = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < (int)rideWindow; ++i) {
    const int k = i;
    double laggedUpper = upperHistory[(bandCursor + upperHistory.size() - (std::size_t)k) % upperHistory.size()];
    double laggedLower = lowerHistory[(bandCursor + lowerHistory.size() - (std::size_t)k) % lowerHistory.size()];
    if (el_gt(close[k], laggedUpper)) {
        rideUpCount = rideUpCount + 1;
    }
    if (el_lt(close[k], laggedLower)) {
        rideDownCount = rideDownCount + 1;
    }
}
bandCursor = (bandCursor + 1) % upperHistory.size();
// The deepest lagged read is upper[rideWindow - 1].
countReady = ctx.CurrentBar() > (int)rideWindow - 1;
